             <h4>Why</h4>
             <p>In ELECTRE III, concordance captures the degree to which criteria support an outranking relation. Unlike simple weighted sums, ELECTRE separates concordance (positive evidence) from discordance (veto evidence). This separation allows minority criteria with strong opposition to block an outranking even when the majority supports it.</p>
